# Scenario psg-log-assert-mismatch (plan 05-09, D-20): outcome guest-fail, exit 10. The original
# diagnostic never writes a PSG register, so its write log is empty; this assert says one record,
# so the failing clause is named in the detail. It shows that the new assert subject cannot pass
# vacuously: a wrong count over an empty log fails.
# expect-detail: assert=1 line=14 psglog count == 1 got 0
ivss 1
id psg-log-assert-mismatch
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub
content grom zero-grom
content cart diag-cpu-1.ivsc
capture psglog
run-to 4000 cpu-cycles stop halted
assert psglog count == 1
